From: =?utf-8?q?Maxime_B=C3=A9lair?= <maxime.belair@canonical.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Apr 2026 10:24:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] parser: refactor compressed policy cache
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Previously, policies used a "normal" cache for uncompressed policies and
a dedicated compressed/ directory for compressed policies, increasing
the overall storage footprint.

Now, only a single cache file is present. The parser detects whether
it's compressed or not through its header, improving disk efficiency,
which is particularly useful on constrained systems.

Signed-off-by: Maxime Bélair <maxime.belair@canonical.com>
